@* FAQ — an Accordion. Each item is a <details>, so the fold is the browser's: it works with no
   script, it is in the page for a crawler, and the chevron turns on [open].

   Same Name on each AccordionItem = type="single": opening one closes the others. Leave the
   Name off for independent toggles. *@

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-16">
    <div class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">Everything else lives in the docs.</p>
    </div>

    <Accordion Class="mt-10">
        @foreach (var f in Faqs)
        {
            <AccordionItem Name="faq" Open="@(f.Open)">
                <AccordionTrigger>@f.Question</AccordionTrigger>
                <AccordionContent>@f.Answer</AccordionContent>
            </AccordionItem>
        }
    </Accordion>
</section>

@code {
    record Faq(string Question, string Answer, bool Open = false);

    static readonly Faq[] Faqs =
    [
        new("Is this actually shadcn/ui?", "Yes. Same tokens, same class strings, same data-slot on every root, same ARIA. The classes are generated from shadcn's own source and checked against it by a test.", true),
        new("Does it need JavaScript?", "The library ships one file that wires the few things a native element cannot do — popovers, the select panel, tab switching. With it disabled, every form still posts and every link still navigates."),
        new("How is it different from the React version?", "Static SSR renders once; Unpoly swaps fragments. There is no client state, so state lives in native elements, the URL, or a cookie — whichever the platform already has."),
        new("Can I use it with an existing Blazor app?", "Yes. Add the package, put the script tags in the head, and start writing components. It does not require an interactive render mode."),
        new("How do themes work?", "A theme is a [data-theme] block of custom properties. The demo ships seventy of them, from Vercel to Cupertino, and a live Customizer that prints the block to paste."),
    ];
}
